# Keys for test runs. Copy to .env (gitignored) and fill in; never commit .env.
# Read by `dub recognize` and by Debug builds of the app. Release builds never
# read it, and a key typed in Preferences wins over it.

# Dub's AcoustID *application* key (acoustid.org/new-application), sent with
# every lookup. Not the account's API key: that one submits fingerprints in a
# person's name, and Dub never submits.
DUB_ACOUSTID_KEY=

# Your Apple developer team ID (developer.apple.com → Membership, ten
# characters). With an "Apple Development" certificate in the keychain,
# `make app` and the Swift tests sign with it, and macOS keeps the
# microphone grant across rebuilds instead of asking after every one.
# Without the certificate it is ignored and the app is signed ad hoc.
DUB_TEAM_ID=
